# Southbrook Wall Display — Caddy snippet
#
# Drop this into alfacore-caddy's Caddyfile (or import it from a
# separate file). Implements the routes spec §8.3 + §11.
#
# WHAT IT DOES:
#   - Serves the kiosk HTML from /data/southbrook-wall/ (which the
#     operator populates via `rsync services/southbrook_wall/wall/
#     <caddy-data-mount>/southbrook-wall/`).
#   - Proxies /wall/api/* to southbrook-odoo on the southbrook docker
#     network — that's where the JSON feeds live
#     (/southbrook/wall/<station>.json controllers).
#   - Serves a static fallback at /wall/static/ for graceful degrade
#     when Odoo is mid-restart or unreachable. A cron drops fresh
#     snapshots here every 60s (set up separately).
#
# OPERATOR INSTALL (one-time):
#
#   1. Drop the HTML pages on the QNAP:
#        rsync -av services/southbrook_wall/wall/ \
#          /share/CACHEDEV3_DATA/Container/alfacore/data/southbrook-wall/
#      Or however your alfacore-caddy data volume is bind-mounted.
#
#   2. Open alfacore-caddy's Caddyfile and either:
#        a) PASTE the snippet below verbatim, OR
#        b) Add `import southbrook_wall` near the top, then put this
#           snippet's contents in a sibling file named `southbrook_wall`.
#
#   3. Inside your site block (or new site block for display.southbrookcabinetry.space):
#        display.southbrookcabinetry.space {
#            import southbrook_wall_routes
#        }
#
#   4. Reload Caddy IN-PLACE (per [[qnap_caddyfile_bind_mount_trap]]
#      use cp overwrite, never mv):
#        docker exec alfacore-caddy caddy reload --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#
#   5. Visit the URL from your shop's LAN:
#        http://display.southbrookcabinetry.space/wall/shipping
#      Should render the dock kiosk with live data.
#
# IP ALLOWLIST DECISION (spec §7.8) DEFERRED:
#   The wall feeds are currently `auth='public'` in the addon. Until
#   you've decided whether to LAN-allowlist or Cloudflare-Access-gate
#   these routes, anyone who can reach display.southbrookcabinetry.space
#   can read the SO numbers + customer names. Make that decision
#   before pointing this at a public hostname. The simplest gate is
#   adding a `@allowed_ips { remote_ip 10.0.0.0/8 }` matcher and
#   wrapping the routes with it.

(southbrook_wall_routes) {
    # Wall kiosk HTML pages (static, served by Caddy from disk).
    # The /wall/shipping URL resolves to /data/southbrook-wall/shipping/index.html
    handle_path /wall/shipping* {
        root * /data/southbrook-wall/shipping
        try_files {path} {path}/ /index.html
        file_server
    }

    # JSON feed — proxied to the Odoo controller. The kiosk JS calls
    # /wall/api/<station>.json; we map that to /southbrook/wall/<station>.json
    # on the Odoo backend.
    handle /wall/api/* {
        # Strip /wall/api/ prefix, prepend /southbrook/wall/
        rewrite * /southbrook/wall{path}
        rewrite /southbrook/wall/wall/api/* /southbrook/wall/{1}
        reverse_proxy southbrook-odoo:8069 {
            header_up Host {host}
            header_up X-Forwarded-For {remote}
        }
    }

    # Static-fallback JSON (cron-dropped snapshots). Serves the most
    # recent dump when Odoo is unreachable.
    handle_path /wall/static/* {
        root * /data/southbrook-wall/static
        file_server
    }
}
